      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 687106299,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "@chuckcraft sorry I couldn't get at this sooner. But as a general question, MainStatusBar gets the capture file through setFilename, as well as by utilizing wsApp->mainWindow .. . Why not add a slot to captureEvent instead? It would avoid cannibalizing another function which is not really used for this, and change the appropriate texts at the right time - namely when the capture is really closing",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9e1d973c5007651b2ca47071f80324c2de5349d873e365cf0761df5542dfe382?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rknall"
